component AgentConfig {
  goal {
    Load and validate the spike's agent configuration so that every other component
    receives an agent definition whose skills are absolute folders.
  }

  state {
    The configuration is one *agent file*, .agents/subzero.yaml, with a skills map
    from skill name to *skill folder*, an endpoints map and an agents map of named
    *agent definition* entries.

    The endpoints map holds an entry for a *model endpoint*. A model endpoint
    is the part of the model of an agent definition before its first slash, and
    each agent definition belongs to the model endpoint of its model. The entry
    holds the *parallel limit* of that model endpoint, a positive whole number
    that is the most child runs that one process runs at the same time on it. A
    model endpoint with no entry has no parallel limit, and every
    agent definition on the same model endpoint shares its parallel limit.

    An agent definition has a description, a host that is always pi, a model, a
    *thinking level*, the names of its skills, a *tool list* and a *timeout*.

    The timeout is a required number of seconds. It limits the wall-clock time of
    a child run from its spawn to its settlement, including skill verification,
    and it does not run while the child run is Pending.
  }

  logic {
    On load, read the agent file, validate every agent definition against the
    schema, and resolve each skill folder relative to the directory of the
    agent file into an absolute path. The flow returns the validated agent
    definitions to its caller, or stops with a *load error* that names the
    offending agent definition, or says that the agent file is missing,
    unreadable or malformed. One invalid agent definition fails the whole load.
  }

  constraints {
    An agent definition must be rejected, naming it, when its host is not pi or
    when its host is pi and it has no model.

    An endpoints entry must be rejected with a load error that names its
    model endpoint when its parallel limit is not a positive whole number, or
    when no agent definition belongs to its model endpoint.

    An agent definition must be rejected, naming it, when it has no timeout or its
    timeout is not a positive number of seconds.

    An agent definition that names a skill missing from the skills map must be
    rejected with the agent and the skill both named.

    A skill folder that does not exist on disk must still load. The missing folder
    is reported only when a child is launched.

    AgentConfig must read the agent file again on each call that asks for an
    agent definition, so that an edit to it is picked up without a restart.

    AgentConfig must read only the one agent file. It must not merge layers, write
    subzero.lock or ask for repo trust in the spike, because those belong to the
    agent definition format of a later version.

    AgentConfig resolves the *project root* from SUBZERO_PROJECT_DIR first,
    then from the roots that the parent adapter reports, and for the command
    line from its working directory. It must never use the working directory of
    the server process. It keeps no project root between calls, because
    DelegationService asks once for each process and hands the answer to the
    other components. It finds the agent file under the project root that its
    caller hands over.

    An empty SUBZERO_PROJECT_DIR counts as unset. When the parent adapter
    reports several roots, the first one reported wins. The project root must
    be an absolute path with its symbolic links resolved. When no source gives
    a project root, AgentConfig must return an *unresolved root error* that
    names SUBZERO_PROJECT_DIR as the setting to fix, and must resolve again on
    the next call.
  }

  cases {
    A valid file with one pi agent definition loads, and its skill folder entries
    are absolute paths.

    An unknown host value is rejected, and the error names the agent definition
    that holds it.

    A name that is not configured gives an unknown agent error that lists every
    configured agent definition.

    With no SUBZERO_PROJECT_DIR and no root reported by the parent adapter, the
    project root is not resolved and the caller gets the unresolved root error.

    Two agent definitions on the model endpoint r9700, whose entry has a
    parallel limit of 1, are both given that parallel limit of 1, and an
    agent definition on a model endpoint with no entry is given none. An entry
    for r9770 that no agent definition belongs to gives a load error that names
    r9770.

    An agent file with one invalid agent definition gives a load error that names
    it and returns no agent definition, not even a valid one.
  }

  interface {
    Provide each configured agent definition by name, with its thinking level, its
    tool list, its timeout and every skill folder resolved to an absolute folder.

    Provide the model endpoint of each agent definition with the parallel limit
    of that model endpoint, or none when its entry is missing.

    List the names of every configured agent definition so that a caller can report
    them in an error.

    Return an *unknown agent error* that names the unknown name and every
    configured agent definition when a name is not configured, so that a front end
    can show it.

    Return a load error that names the invalid agent definition, or says that the
    agent file is missing, unreadable or malformed, so that a front end can show
    it.

    Provide the project root for a caller in the order the constraints give, or
    return the unresolved root error when no source gives one.
  }

  decisions {
    Skill folders resolve against the directory of the agent file and not the
    working directory, so the same file behaves the same from the server, the
    command line and the experiment harness.
  }
}
